{"title":"BrightStep Tutoring","sub":"How big is the market for paid maths tutoring?","type":"Market sizing","industry":"Education","geo":"United Kingdom","diff":1,"fmt":"Candidate-led","time":"25-30 min","skills":"Segmented market sizing · sanity checks","prompt":"BrightStep is a start-up offering live online maths lessons in small groups for secondary school pupils in England. Its investors want to know how big the paid maths tutoring market is, and whether BrightStep's target of $10M revenue in three years is realistic.","clarify":[{"q":"Which pupils?","a":"Secondary pupils, years 7 to 11 (ages 11 to 16), in England."},{"q":"Which spending counts?","a":"Money families pay for maths tutoring, online or in person. Leave out school-funded tutoring for now."},{"q":"BrightStep's price?","a":"$12 per 60-minute small-group lesson. One-to-one tutors typically charge around $35 an hour."},{"q":"Data available?","a":"Yes: the interviewer has pupil numbers and survey data on who pays for tutoring."}],"structure":{"root":"Annual spend on paid maths tutoring","branches":[{"head":"Who pays","items":["Secondary pupils in England","Share whose families pay for maths tutoring","Differences by household income"]},{"head":"How much they buy","items":["Sessions per year (term-time weekly?)","Price per session"]},{"head":"BrightStep's slice","items":["Families who'd choose small groups over one-to-one","Price gap: $12 vs $35"]}]},"hypothesis":"I'd expect a market in the hundreds of millions of dollars: a few hundred thousand tutored pupils, paying weekly through the school year.","questions":[{"q":"Here is the interviewer's data. Estimate the annual market.","exhibit":{"kind":"chart","svg":"<svg xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" width=\"393.851281pt\" height=\"168.724pt\" viewBox=\"0 0 393.851281 168.724\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" version=\"1.1\"><defs><style type=\"text/css\">*{stroke-linejoin: round; stroke-linecap: butt}</style></defs><g id=\"figure_1\"><g i